  "row_count": 20,
  "notes": {
    "raw": "\\*Data except enthalpy of formation at 298 K estimated. \nPhase changes: 903.9 K, melting point of Sb; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 4.750$ kcal/mol. \n1860 K, boiling point of Sb to equilibrium mixture of $Sb(g)$ , $Sb_{2}(g)$ , and $Sb_{4}(g)$ . \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n298.15-3000 K: $Cp^{\\circ} = 31.478 + 0.154 \\times 10^{-3} T - 3.802 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$ \n$H^{0}-H_{298}^{0}=31.478\\times10^{-3}T+0.077\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+3.802\\times10^{2}T^{-1}-10.667$ \nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n298.15-903.9 K: $\\Delta \\mathrm{Hr}^{\\circ} = -15.069 + 3.699 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 3.919 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 342.550 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -15.069 - 3.699 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 3.919 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 171.275 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} + 46.720 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \n903.9-1860 K: $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -25.579 - 3.537 \\times 10^{-3} T - 0.403 \\times 10^{-6} T^{2} + 277.750 T^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -25.579 + 3.537 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 0.403 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 138.875 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} + 12.312 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \nSource: Data based on Prusaczyk (101) who estimated molecular constants. ",
    "lines_raw": [
      "\\*Data except enthalpy of formation at 298 K estimated.",
      "Phase changes: 903.9 K, melting point of Sb; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 4.750$ kcal/mol.",
      "1860 K, boiling point of Sb to equilibrium mixture of $Sb(g)$ , $Sb_{2}(g)$ , and $Sb_{4}(g)$ .",
      "Heat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations:",
      "298.15-3000 K: $Cp^{\\circ} = 31.478 + 0.154 \\times 10^{-3} T - 3.802 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$",
      "$H^{0}-H_{298}^{0}=31.478\\times10^{-3}T+0.077\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+3.802\\times10^{2}T^{-1}-10.667$",
      "Reaction equations (kcal/mol):",
      "298.15-903.9 K: $\\Delta \\mathrm{Hr}^{\\circ} = -15.069 + 3.699 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 3.919 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 342.550 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$",
      "$\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -15.069 - 3.699 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 3.919 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 171.275 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} + 46.720 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$",
      "903.9-1860 K: $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -25.579 - 3.537 \\times 10^{-3} T - 0.403 \\times 10^{-6} T^{2} + 277.750 T^{-1}$",
